    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Outside restaurant Claude Monet in the third episode. A stern prosecutor named Vadim confronts Max and demands to know who Vika is dating. Listen to their tense conversation in Russian first, and then we will break it down together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Слышь, малой, есть разговор.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Что вам нужно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Тут у вас работает Вика.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Виктория Сергеевна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "С кем она тут встречается?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Ну, почему молчим?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Почему я должен отвечать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Не хочешь отвечать здесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Ответишь у меня в прокуратуре.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Ты меня понял?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понял, всё понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она ни с кем не встречается.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Ну, смотри у меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надо срочно предупредить всех.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's examine this threatening interrogation step by step.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Слышь, малой, есть разговор.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Listen, kid, I want to talk.' A gruff stranger corners Max outside the restaurant.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Что вам нужно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What do you need?' Max responds cautiously to the aggressive tone.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Тут у вас работает Вика.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vika works here with you.' the speaker uses the classic Russian possession phrasing — literally 'at you' rather than a verb meaning 'to have', pairing it with 'here' and 'works'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Виктория Сергеевна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Viktoria Sergeyevna.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'Viktoria' directly with 'Sergeyevna', combining 'Viktoria' with 'Sergeyevna'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "С кем она тут встречается?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Who is she seeing here?' the speaker puts the word for 'here' together with 'is dating' in a crisp, natural spoken turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Ну, почему молчим?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, why are we silent?' Here the speaker anchors the line on the word meaning 'why' and builds the thought around 'are silent'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Почему я должен отвечать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why should I answer?' The phrasing opens with 'why' before bringing in 'must' and 'to answer' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Не хочешь отвечать здесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Don't want to answer here?' , combining 'want' with 'to answer' and 'here'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Ответишь у меня в прокуратуре.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You'll answer in my prosecutor's office.' , combining 'will answer' with 'prosecutor's office'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Ты меня понял?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you understand me?' the speaker turns a statement into a question purely through rising intonation on the word meaning 'understood' to make the point directly in conversation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понял, всё понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Understood, understood everything.' Max delivers a punchy conversational reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'understood'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она ни с кем не встречается.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She is not seeing anyone.' Max protects Vika and himself with a firm denial.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vadim",
      "t": "Ну, смотри у меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, you watch yourself.' the speaker uses the classic Russian possession phrasing — literally 'at me' rather than a verb meaning 'to have', followed by 'watch'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надо срочно предупредить всех.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Must urgently warn everyone.' Here Max anchors the line on the word meaning 'necessary' and builds the thought around 'urgently' and 'to warn'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
